        <p>A LANCASHIRE MAN'S EVIDENCE. Mr. Ch.rles Bubb, a ticket collector in the service of determined that she should try them. I went to Mr the Lancashire and Yorkshire Railway Compan7, Ii- Sherratts, chemist, Qdeen's.road, and got a box of Dr re:iiing at 37, Eau/ran-street, Newton Reath, detailed Williams' Piult Pills. Talking to the chemist about them to the Manchester reporter, the following concerning his be said they were very good pills. Well, I sent the box wife : to my wife privately, and told her to take thern,ancl let "My wife," he said, "ii thirty-one years cf age. She me know their effect. Sae used that box, and wrote resides with our two children it No 9, Lickhill-itree, telling me they seemed to be doing her good. Pleased Stourport, Worcestershue, as she was net able tr_ come at the result, I sent her a second box. The improvement here when I did. After the birth of her second child, continued day by day. She got a third box, and to cut he became very ill. Her lice turned a pale Ye the story short. I may till you that the three boxes sllow, her cheeks were thin eyes dull, and she suffered from completely cured her. After being ill and under medical langour and general !exhaustion. She aas in tia con. treatment for a whole year, she was cured by three dition to take up her residence in this dull, monotonous boxes of Dr Williams' Pink Pills for Pale People.",! Manchester. Months passed by and there was no " How long is it since she regained her former health —,nsulted a local doctor, who told and strength? " .. .. _ _ . 'ls ago. ''''''</p>
