        <p>Nervous dia-irlers are gelerally traceable to defective digestion. Most nervous people are dyspeptic also. The stomach does nit digest the food ; the necesary supply of vital particles which the blood should recei from properly digested food fails, and the result iv fair almost immediately upon the most sensitive portions of the human organism—the Nerves. Impure blond irritates the nerves and causes nervous weaknes,. This readers the nervous system very liable to be affected by unhealthy influences. In nine cases cut:of ten, if the imperfect digestion be remedied, the nervousness and weakness will disappear. The only certain remedy is lytaa Evans' Qainine Bitters, sold everywhere in bottles 23. and 43. 6). each, or will be sent, carriage free, on receipt of stamps, direct, by the Sole Propriet- ors :—Thd Quinine Bitters Manufacturing Company, Limited, Llanelly, South Wales. Beware of Imita- tions. The name " Garilym scans" must be found en the label, on the scamp, and on the blttle, to ensure its being genuine. Be sure mou get the right article when you ask for it. Do not be put off with substitutes. No ther preparation is " Just as good "or " Tne same biog."</p>
