        <p>WARRINGTON. Local Conservatism. A meeting of the council of the Conservative Association was held on Monday evening in the Assembly R 30122 at the Conservative Club when Mr John White presided. Councillor John Roberts, in eulogistic terms, proposed the re-election of Mr White as chairman for the ensuing year.—Mr Jenkins seconded and the motion was carried and Mr White briefly replied.—Cauneillor Greening pro- posed and Alderman Heaton seconded a vote of thanks to Mr White for his services and it was carried:—Councillor Smethurst proposed the re- election of Alderman Francomb as vice-chairman of the council and said they regretted the state of his health would not permit him to be present that evening. They all sympathised with him in his illness and hoped he would soon be restored to health.—Councillor Baird seconded and the motion was carried.—The Finance and General Committee , having been re-appointed the council proceeded to ' discuss the steps to be taken in the approaching municipal elections.</p>
