        <p>Runcorn 'A " v. Oldham " This fixture was played off on the Rtinccra On Saturday atteinoon, and attracted a fail attendance. The visitors brought wish them ' old hands who have done duty in the first teard.4 the start, Runcorn pressed strongly, but were a`, a steady defence. Taylor, taking advantage old by Brown, scored a soft try for the visitors, an, , kicked a goal. Runcorn again attacked, and several passing movements, but these efforts ' to collapse at the critical moment, and no an accrued. Runcorn continued to have much tbe the play, and several times came witlao of scoring. They had failed, bowel' pierce _the _Oldham line when half</p>
