      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-10-18_WidnesExaminer_art0080" n="art0080">
        <head>Radcliffe v. Widnes.</head>
        <p>Radcliffe v. Widnes.</p>
        <p>At Rlckliffe. In the fuss halt Widnes had the best of the game, during which Hampson and Moss scored tries, and Douglas dropped a goal. Peacock added a try afterwards, while Platt got over for Radcliffe. Re- sult i—Widnes one goal, four tries (14 points) ; Rad- cliffe one try (3 points). Wigan v. Rochdale Hornets. At Wigan, before 4,000 spectators. Rigby scored for Wigan, and Griorod kicked a penalty goal on behalf of the visitors. The Hornets played hard to equalise, but Rigby and Yates again scored flr Wigan, vino won by one goal three tries (11 points); to Rochdale Hornets one goal (2 points). Barrow v. Morecambe. -•-</p>
        <p>At Barrow. --A.ft;r—pre- s'ain—g for some time Barrow scored through Bowker, the same player kicking a goal. In Ode second ball tue home team again played well, but could not add to their score. Result :—Barrow, one goal, one try (5 ooints) ; Morecambe, nil. Altrincham v Whilom.</p>
        <p>At Altrincham.llom immediately began to press, and Young ran in an easy try, riter two minutes' play. Eagera failed at goal. Austin afterwards made •</p>
