        <p>WARRING TON.</p>
        <p>Funeral of the Late Mr. J. Mawson. Amid many marks of respect, the remains of the late Mr John Mawson, principal of the firm of Messrs Mawson and Company,tailor and outfitters, Sankey-street, were interred in the Warrington Cemetery on Sunday afternoon, The officiating clergyman was the Rev W Bracecanap, curate of St Peter's. The chief mourners were Mr Stanley. Mawson (son), Mr Taylor, Mr Cooper, Mr Morton and Mr J Bailey. Representatives attended from the Gilbert Greenall Lodge (No. 1250) of Masons, the Manchester Unity of Oddfellows and the Angler' Association. A large number of people assembled at the graveside to pay a last tribute of respect to the deceased. The coffin bore the in- scription " John Alawson,aged 58, died October 9t,b, 1901." A latge number of brautiful floral tributes was received,among them being wreaths from the Admiral Nelson Lodge of Oddfellows and the Angling Association. The funeral arrangements were carried out by Messrs J Emson and Son.</p>
